Short:    Sega Mega Drive/Genesis, SMS, GG emulator for PiStorm
Author:   Pedro Cotter
Uploader: Pedro Cotter
Type:     misc/emu
Version:  1.9
Requires: PiStorm/Emu68, AmigaOS 3.x or CaffeineOS, RTG (P96 or CGX)
Architecture: m68k-amigaos


GenesisPlusGX v1.9 for AmigaOS 3.x / CaffeineOS
================================================

A Sega Mega Drive / Genesis, Master System, Game Gear and SG-1000
emulator for PiStorm/Emu68 systems, built on the Genesis Plus GX
core by Eke-Eke (based on Genesis Plus by Charles MacDonald).
Amiga port by Pedro Cotter.


Requirements
------------

- PiStorm with Emu68
- AmigaOS 3.x or CaffeineOS
- RTG: Picasso96 or CyberGraphX
- Chip RAM for the Paula audio buffers
- Optional: MUI 3.8 for the launcher
- Optional: AHI for sound cards
- Optional, for GPU output: Pi 4 / CM4 and minigl.library 29.1
  (PiStorm3D). CaffeineOS already includes the library.


Installation
------------

1. Copy GenesisPlusGX and GenesisPlusGX-Launcher into one drawer.
2. Put ROMs anywhere. The launcher browses these drawers:
     PROGDIR:Roms/               Mega Drive / Genesis
     PROGDIR:Roms/Gamegear/      Game Gear
     PROGDIR:Roms/Mastersystem/  Master System
3. Start a game from the launcher, or from the Shell (see Usage).

PROGDIR:GenesisPlusGX.cfg is created on the first run. Both the
emulator and the launcher read it; the launcher writes it.
See Manual.txt for the full guide.


Usage
-----

  GenesisPlusGX <romfile> [options]

  The ROM comes first. Options start with a dash and override the
  config file for this run only.

  Video:
    -scanlines      Scanlines, medium (2x mode)
    -scanlines=N    Scanline level 1-3 (1=subtle 2=medium 3=strong)
    -vsync          Wait for vertical blank (costs speed)
    -screendepth=N  32 (default) or 16 (Zorro RTG cards)

  Audio:
    -14bit          14-bit Paula stereo (4 channels)
    -paulafreq=N    Paula rate in Hz (default 41243; 0 = 27710)
    -ahi            AHI audio (sound cards)
    -ahifreq=N      AHI rate: 22050, 27710, 32000, 44100
    -paulafilter    Force the audio (LED) filter on (~7 kHz)
    -nosound        No audio

  Cheats (Mega Drive only):
    -cheats         Apply PROGDIR:Cheats/<romname>.cht (default)
    -nocheats       Ignore the cheat file for this run

  Performance:
    -frameskip=N    Draw 1 of N+1 frames (0-5)
    -autoskip       Skip drawing when behind schedule (default)
    -noautoskip     Never skip automatically
    -fps            FPS counter in the top-right corner
    -nodrc          Virtua Racing: DSP interpreter, not recompiler

  GPU output (Pi 4 / CM4, minigl.library 29.1):
    -gl             Draw through the V3D GPU
    -nogl           Normal display even if glout=1 in the config
    -gleffect=N     0=sharp 1=smooth 2=scanlines 3=composite blend
    -glsize=WxH     Screen size (default 640x480)
    -glrgba         Upload RGBA8 instead of RGB565

  Examples:
    GenesisPlusGX Roms/Sonic2.md
    GenesisPlusGX Roms/OutRun.md -14bit -fps
    GenesisPlusGX Roms/SoR2.zip -ahi -ahifreq=44100
    GenesisPlusGX Roms/Comix.md -gl -gleffect=3


Controls
--------

  Player 1 keyboard        Player 2 numpad
  Arrow keys  D-Pad        8 2 4 6       D-Pad
  1           A            0             A
  2           B            .             B
  3           C            Enter         C
  Q W E       X Y Z        Help          Start
  Space/Return Start

  Joystick or CD32 pad: joystick port = player 1, mouse port =
  player 2. CD32 pad: Red=A Blue=B Green=C Yellow=X Reverse=Y
  Forward=Z Play=Start. A plain joystick gives A and B.

  Master System / Game Gear use A and B as buttons 1 and 2.
  Keys can be remapped in the config file or the launcher.

  F5  Save state     F8  Load state     Esc  Quit


Save States / SRAM
------------------

  F5 saves to PROGDIR:States/<romname>.gsx, F8 loads it.
  Battery-backed SRAM is saved to PROGDIR:States/<romname>.srm on
  exit (and on F5) and loaded again on the next start.


Cheats
------

  RetroArch .cht files (Game Genie and address:data codes), Mega
  Drive only, in PROGDIR:Cheats/<romname>.cht. Turn entries on and
  off on the launcher's Cheats page, or set cheatN_enable = true in
  the file.


Audio
-----

  paula (default)  8-bit stereo, 41243 Hz, lowest CPU cost.
  14bit            14-bit stereo on all four Paula channels
                   (volume 64 + volume 1 pairs, started in sync).
  ahi              16-bit stereo through AHI.

  On a 15 kHz native display, Paula cannot fetch samples faster than
  about 28 kHz (HRM: minimum period 124). If the exit summary says
  Paula played slower than its nominal rate, use -paulafreq=27710.

  Run from a Shell to see the exit summary: frames drawn, frames over
  budget, audio frames dropped or run dry.


Video
-----

  Opens an RTG screen, 32-bit by default. screendepth=16 (or
  -screendepth=16) halves the blit bandwidth (for Zorro RTG
  cards). Scanline levels 1-3.

  GPU output (glout=1 or -gl, Pi 4 / CM4 only) draws the picture
  through the V3D GPU with minigl.library 29.1: any screen size,
  scanlines and a composite blend. CaffeineOS already includes the
  library; elsewhere install it from the PiStorm3D release. It looks
  better but is not faster (about 6 ms of CPU per frame), so keep
  autoskip on. The picture is still a little soft; this is open.


Formats
-------

  .bin .gen .md .smd  Mega Drive / Genesis
  .sms                Master System
  .gg                 Game Gear
  .sg                 SG-1000
  .rom                any of the above
  .zip                a zip holding one of the above

  Maximum ROM size 8 MB. Sega CD is not supported.


Configuration (defaults)
------------------------

  audio=paula        paula / 14bit / ahi / off
  paulafreq=41243    ahifreq=44100
  hqfm=1             0 = linear FM resampling, much faster
  hqpsg=1            0 = linear PSG resampling, faster
  screendepth=32     16 for Zorro RTG cards
  glout=0            gleffect=1    glsize=640x480
  scanlines=0        vsync=0       frameskip=0
  autoskip=1         fps=1         cheats=1
  fmvol=60           psgvol=60
  paulafilter=0      paulaboost=1  paulastereo=1
  ahiboost=0

  paulamargin and ahimargin from older versions are ignored.
  Delete the file to get the defaults back.


Changes
-------

  v1.9 (11.10.2026)
  - The video and VDP assembler loops no longer use DBF. With
    Emu68's "slow DBF" option on they ran up to about a third
    slower per instruction (measured on a CM4); now that option
    makes no difference.
  - Virtua Racing: the DSP recompiler handles short subroutine
    calls inside its blocks (no measurable speed change).

  v1.8 (10.10.2026)
  - Virtua Racing: the SVP DSP program is recompiled into 68k
    code (Emu68 only). Race 57-60 fps on a CM4 (about 33
    before); DSP time 13.5 -> 5.4 ms per frame.
  - Faster DSP interpreter when the recompiler is off (-nodrc).

  v1.7 (09.10.2026)
  - Frames paced against an exact EClock schedule; audio buffers
    hold exactly one frame and the queue depth is rate-controlled.
    No more gaps from timer jitter; paulamargin/ahimargin obsolete.
  - 14-bit Paula: all four channels start in sync, symmetric
    HI/LO split, table-driven converter.
  - Optional GPU output through PiStorm3D minigl.library.
  - Autoskip only skips when more than half a frame behind.
  - Launcher 1.2: Cheats page, GPU output settings, margin
    sliders removed.
  - Exit summary with audio and frame timing counters.
  - paulafilter=1 now turns the audio filter on (it turned it
    off before).

  v1.6 (06.07.2026)
  - Player 2 input fixed.
  - screendepth=16, hqfm and hqpsg options.
  - AHI rounding headroom, 8-bit rounding, stuck keys fixed.

  See README.md for older versions.


